# Landing page motion

- Use `motion` (`motion/react`), already a dependency. Do not add another animation library.
- Wrap sections below the hero in `<Reveal>` (`@/components/motion/reveal`) so they fade up + in as they
  scroll into view. For grids of cards/features/stats, use `<Reveal stagger>` with `<RevealItem>` children.
- Hero content animates once on mount (`fadeUp`/`fadeIn` from `@/lib/motion`), not on scroll — it's
  already in the viewport on load.
- Standard entrance: opacity 0→1 + translateY 24px→0, 0.5–0.6s, `EASE_OUT` from `@/lib/motion`. Reuse the
  shared variants; don't invent new durations/easings per section.
- Stagger siblings 0.08–0.12s apart (`staggerContainer` default). Don't stagger more than ~6 direct
  children — batch larger grids into rows instead.
- Always respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. `<Reveal>` already disables itself via `useReducedMotion()` —
  don't bypass it with a raw `motion.div`.
- Keep it subtle: no bounce/spring, no rotation, no flicker. This is product/marketing motion, not a game.
